PART 13 — IMPORTANT INTERPRETATION NOTES

For Block 5 option fingerprints, the numeric scores mean:

How much the option supports or satisfies that sensitivity dimension

Examples:

High vulnerabilityProtectionSensitivity score on an option means the option strongly protects vulnerable people.
High outcomeAggregationSensitivity score means the option strongly maximizes total benefit or total people helped.
High directnessSensitivity score means the option better avoids direct harsh harm or highly intrusive intervention.
High contextSensitivity score means the option is more context-aware or nuanced.
High gainResponsivenessSensitivity score means the option is more responsive to efficiency, scarce-resource preservation, or broader system incentives.
High stakeholderPerspectiveShiftSensitivity score means the option better integrates multiple stakeholder viewpoints.
High groupSizeSensitivity score means the option pays more attention to how many people are affected.

Use this interpretation consistently in the ranking logic and the UI explanations.

